    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22504" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-cōnīvens</span></b>  (also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inconnīvens</span></b> ),
		entis, adj.
		2. in-conniveo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that does not close the eyes</i> (late Lat.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">stare solitus Socrates dicitur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					2, 1, 2</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, of the eye, <i>that does
				not close</i>, <i>unclosing</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">justitiae oculus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 29, 2, 20</span></i>
			. 
			</div>
